      "writtenOn": "2018-05-17T16:36:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This method is also used in DcTracker so I\u0027m marking it as @hide. This method is moved from DcTracker.parsetypes: https://cs.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/opt/telephony/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DcTracker.java?type\u003dcs\u0026q\u003ddctracker.parse+package:%5Eandroid$\u0026g\u003d0\u0026l\u003d1837\nwhere emtpy string is converted to \"*\". \n\nNow as you mentioned ApnEditor has prevented empty string, what about other sources of APN? E.g. from the SIM database? If there can be empty string for APN type from other sources then it\u0027s better to keep the original behavior? Otherwise it\u0027s definitely better to return 0 for empty string.",
      "parentUuid": "b9d4dff1_dc615bae",
      "range": {
